+## Delegate repository changes to Horde
+
+First determine whether you are already a Horde worker. If HORDE_WORKER_TOKEN
+is set or the runtime gave you a worker identity and an assigned Horde step,
+follow the horde-worker skill and perform that step. Do not
+resubmit the assignment as a new root task.
+
+For the agent talking to the user: for every user-requested repository change,
+use the horde skill and delegate implementation, tests, and review to Horde. This
+includes small edits, documentation, bug fixes, features, and refactoring, and
+overrides the skill's default advice to handle small edits locally. Do not
+implement changes directly or substitute another subagent system unless the
+user explicitly requests it. Read-only investigation and answering questions
+may happen in the current session.
+
+The agent talking to the user owns clarification, task submission, monitoring,
+answering worker questions within the user's instructions, and inspecting
+results. Include the user's constraints and acceptance checks in the submitted
+task. Follow it until completion or a blocker requiring user input. Verify the
+integrated result and report its branch, checks, and unresolved issues. Keep
+external delivery within the user's authorization.
+
+If Horde is unavailable, report the blocker instead of silently doing the work
+directly.
